# Personal preferences (rename to CLAUDE.local.md - this file is gitignored)

Copy this to `CLAUDE.local.md` in the project root and edit freely.
This file is personal to you and never committed - use it for things
that don't belong in the shared CLAUDE.md.

Examples of what to put here:
- Your local Python environment name / activation command
- Paths specific to your machine (e.g. where you keep the raw CSVs
  if not in data/raw/ for space reasons)
- Personal workflow preferences (e.g. "always show me the plot before
  saving it", "prefer verbose print statements while debugging")
